From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Almeida Barrios <gabarrios2006@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:14:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] api/call-link-join: join a call link as WhatsApp Web does

A WhatsApp Web capture of a call link (2026-11-18: create, query, join alone,
a guest admitted from the waiting room) shows that the link_create,
link_query and link_join stanzas meowcaller builds are the ones WhatsApp Web
sends, and what the joined call needs besides:

- the call entry is incoming (WhatsApp Web's call info says isCaller false),
  with the camera off, like the ongoing-group join; it was outgoing, which
  picks the other relay endpoint, with the camera on for a video link;
- the join ACK carries voip_settings; requestCallNode consumes the ACK before
  onCallAck, so the codec was never selected from it;
- a <heartbeat call-id call-creator/> to <id>@call every 10 s for the whole
  call (waiting-room heartbeat only while waiting); admission used to stop
  the only heartbeat there was;
- roster participants and waiting-room users keep push_name and the guest
  flag: a guest has no user_pn, and its name is all a client can show.

Source of truth: datasheets/voip-call-link-join.md (capture SHA-256
a243f198af1b7729e0cb656238f2317cdb6c13892d6273d8ce02ed2e12280b07)

Validated: signaling/call_link_test.go (heartbeat stanza, captured join ACK,
guest waiting-room user), engine_call_link_test.go (one link_join then only
heartbeats, entry incoming with camera off, roster names, heartbeat stops at
the end, waiting-room heartbeat while waiting); go test ./... green. Not yet
validated on a live call.
