+### api/call-link-join — `implemented`
+
+- Joining a call link builds the call entry as WhatsApp Web holds it after the
+  join (capture of 2026-11-18, `datasheets/voip-call-link-join.md`): direction
+  incoming (`isCaller` false), camera off, the codec from the join ACK's
+  `voip_settings` (which `requestCallNode` takes before `onCallAck`). It used
+  to be outgoing, with the camera on for a video link, and stayed on MLow.
+- A call-link call sends `<heartbeat call-id call-creator/>` to `<id>@call`
+  every 10 s for its whole life, as WhatsApp Web does, admitted or alone; the
+  upstream `type=waiting_room` heartbeat stays while it waits. Admission no
+  longer stops it; the end of the call does.
