+# Datasheet: `api/call-link-join`
+
+Creating a call link, previewing it and joining its call the way WhatsApp
+Web does, and what the call then needs that a group call reached by an offer
+does not: the 10-second `<heartbeat>` and the codec of the join ACK.
+
+**Validation vectors:** focused Go KATs in `signaling/call_link_test.go`
+(the heartbeat stanza, field for field against the capture; the captured join
+ACK, roster and waiting room together) and `engine_call_link_test.go` (the
+join sequence: one `link_join`, no `<accept>`, call entry incoming with the
+camera off, codec from the ACK's `voip_settings`, heartbeat until the call
+ends).
+
+**Reference pinned at:** UNMAPPED — upstream whatsmeow's `call_link.go`
+covers the create/query/join stanzas but not what follows the join. The
+ground truth is a WhatsApp Web capture (2026-11-18, WinZapp's WPPConnect
+engine, stanza recorder on `WAWebDeprecatedSendIqWorkerCompatible`'s
+`deprecatedSendStanzaAndReturnAck`, `WAComms.sendSmaxStanza` and
+`WAWebHandleVoipCall.handleCall`; tags and attributes only, every JID, call
+id and token replaced by a stable alias), capture SHA-256
+`a243f198af1b7729e0cb656238f2317cdb6c13892d6273d8ce02ed2e12280b07`.
+
+## Reference source (verbatim — authoritative)
+
+The account created a voice link, joined it alone, and admitted a guest who
+opened the link in a browser:
+
+```text
+out <call id to="call"><link_create media="audio"/></call>
+ack <ack from="call" class="call" type="link_create" id><link_create media="audio" token="t1"/></ack>
+out <call to="call" id><link_query token="t1" media="audio"/></call>
+ack <ack from="call" class="call" type="link_query" id>
+      <link_query link_creator="j2@lid" link_creator_pn="j3@s.whatsapp.net" media="audio" token="t1">
+        <guest is_guest_eligible="1"/><waiting_room is_admin="1" enabled="0"/>
+      </link_query></ack>
+out <call to="call" id><link_join token="t1" media="audio">
+      <audio enc="opus" rate="16000"/><net medium="2"/><capability ver="1">7 bytes</capability>
+    </link_join></call>
+ack <ack from="call" class="call" type="link_join" id>
+      <group_info call-creator="j2:27@lid" call-id="c4" transaction-id="2" media="audio" connected-limit="32" link-token="t1">
+        <user jid="j2@lid" state="connected" type="admin" user_pn="j3@s.whatsapp.net">
+          <device jid="j2:27@lid" platform="web"><capability ver="1">7 bytes</capability></device></user>
+      </group_info>
+      <waiting_room is_admin="1" link-token="t1" media="audio" call-id="c4" call-creator="j2:27@lid" enabled="0"/>
+      <guest is_guest_eligible="1"/><uploadfieldstat/><voip_settings uncompressed="1">13637 bytes</voip_settings>
+    </ack>
+in  <call from="c4@call" id t><group_update call-creator="j2:27@lid" call-id="c4"><group_info …same roster, device pid="0"…/></group_update></call>
+out <call to="c4@call" id><heartbeat call-id="c4" call-creator="j2:27@lid"/></call>     (every 10 s, the whole call)
+ack <ack from="c4@call" class="call" type="heartbeat" id/>
+in  <call from="c4@call" id t><waiting_room_update call-id="c4" call-creator="j2:27@lid">
+      <waiting_room filter="guests_only" is_admin="1" link-token="t1" media="audio" call-id="c4" call-creator="j2:27@lid" enabled="1" transaction-id="1">
+        <user account_kind="guest" push_name="…" jid="j9@lid" state="waiting_room_joined"/>
+      </waiting_room></waiting_room_update></call>
+out <call to="c4@call" id><waiting_room_admit call-id="c4" call-creator="j2:27@lid"><user jid="j9@lid"/></waiting_room_admit></call>
+ack <ack from="c4@call" class="call" type="waiting_room_admit" id><waiting_room_admit call-id="c4" call-creator="j2:27@lid"/></ack>
+in  <group_update …><group_info … transaction-id="18" link-token="t1" rekey="1">
+      <user j2 connected admin><device j2:27 pid="0"/></user>
+      <user account_kind="guest" push_name="…" jid="j9@lid" state="connected"><device jid="j9@lid" platform="web" pid="1"/></user>
+    </group_info><rte/><relay self_pid="0" …>tokens, auth tokens, key, te2 endpoints, hbh_key</relay><voip_settings/></group_update>
+out <call to="c4@call"><mute_v2 call-id call-creator mute-state="0"/></call>
+out <call to="j9@lid"><transport call-id call-creator transport-message-type="4"><net medium="2" protocol="0"/></transport></call>
+out <call to="j9@lid"><enc_rekey call-id call-creator transaction-id="18"><encopt keygen="2"/><enc v="2" type="pkmsg" count="0"/><device-identity/></enc_rekey></call>
+out <call to="c4@call"><relaylatency …/></call> and <transport transport-message-type="3"><net medium="2"/></transport>
+in  the guest's transport, relaylatency and mute_v2
+```
+
+Call info after the join: `isCaller` false, `isGroupCall` true,
+`callState` CONNECTED_LONELY until someone else connects.
+
+## Go target
+
+```go
+func BuildCallLinkHeartbeat(callID string, callCreator types.JID, requestID string) (waBinary.Node, error)
+func (e *engine) startCallLinkHeartbeat(callID string)
+```
+
+## Implementation notes
+
+- The `link_join` stanza is the one meowcaller already builds: no
+  `<encopt>`, and no `<accept>` follows it.
+- The first account to join a link is the call's creator (`call-creator` is
+  its own device). The server asks it for the group key with `rekey="1"` once
+  someone else connects; the existing fan-out answers that.
+- The call entry is built like the ongoing-group join: direction incoming
+  (`isCaller` false), camera off; the codec comes from the join ACK's
+  `voip_settings`, which `requestCallNode` takes before `onCallAck` sees it.
+- The heartbeat goes to `<call-id>@call` as a JID, every 10 s, admitted or
+  not; while still in the waiting room the upstream `type="waiting_room"`
+  heartbeat is sent instead. It stops when the call ends, not on admission.
+- A guest has no `user_pn` and a device JID without a device number.
